<description>&lt;p&gt;Armed clashes and intercommunal violence continue across South Sudan, with attacks by rebel and SPLA-IO forces targeting civilians in Tonj East, Warrap State and Greater Pibor, while worshippers were attacked in Gorom refugee camp and a teen was killed for refusing an arranged marriage. UNMISS is supporting deterrence efforts in Tonj East and calling for stronger civilian protection during a visit to Unity, and the Gender Ministry has raised concerns about violence against women and children ahead of a 16 Days campaign. President Kiir travelled to Ethiopia and held high-level investment talks with Saudi Arabia in Riyadh, while a US senator warned that Uganda is playing a destabilising role in the country. The Crisis Group urged African intervention to resolve the crisis and the UNDP resident representative issued a message of solidarity. There were 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTFBOTF9pY0NmbXA5N0JTUTJpSl9mdEY4aDExN3hPeENmbUVHRW5NVEpERGxidERUbEVCMWE3LUlPRVdiY1hHa0FLUGxiblhMUk9tQkY1aU04bXdtam0wd2dCMHdJazZHLVpsSER6UURucjMtSXlBTkE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Mail &amp;amp; Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiyAFBVV95cUxPMXNMeVJ1MnEwUVJUa0ZIdnpzN05nVnNFYVpmeE0wZ2QzZktQbTR6Vmp4dncwOGpqeEhhTEg4TWoxNXd0TXRCTTQzaE9RVGJEUG1NZkM0VnU5TlZ3TU5aem9wUXF5djZTWGI2WFlmbHozMFVLck9jb3NlNUJmdzMtVkJWVm5sbUFKdTR0bzlDNTh6eU9saWppc2E0UVluS1J2MEFuVFpFZEJLLUZZMkhOeFJsVnZkY0hSVVJnNnJfaHRxeXNLYlN2Vw?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxOY2xHT3c0cmN2YzNOdnAxN0xiLTNmdFVFcHlVQWdPRF95QUI1S21lME1IallCQWNKSHZKWE91alp4NWljVXVpdnhWUWxreW5CdDdtRl9JRERxcTE0Z0tVNTZzNjhFU2FCVk41bkNXazdPaFdkVWQtYkloUmUyX1R3d280eGhZZlRmV2xsVktFc2Vpd2RmT1NpOUN1bUw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Yeni Safa